WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.782
(orchestral music)

00:00:01.782 --> 00:00:02.813
- The main difficulties

00:00:02.813 --> 00:00:06.971
of working with any
vulnerable or fragile work

00:00:06.971 --> 00:00:08.927
of cultural heritage is the respect

00:00:08.927 --> 00:00:11.996
you have to have for that object.

00:00:11.996 --> 00:00:14.355
Technology is at a point right now

00:00:14.355 --> 00:00:17.811
where we can record the
surface of an object

00:00:17.811 --> 00:00:20.733
down to fractions of a millimeter,

00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:23.623
and it's through this
kind of understanding

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:26.754
that allows you to communicate across time

00:00:26.754 --> 00:00:28.421
and across cultures.

00:00:33.551 --> 00:00:36.165
(frenetic piano music)

00:00:36.165 --> 00:00:40.193
The task of heritage
protection and preservation

00:00:40.193 --> 00:00:41.860
is a real challenge.

00:00:44.013 --> 00:00:46.308
The mission of Factum Foundation

00:00:46.308 --> 00:00:50.814
is to record cultural
heritage, so in the event

00:00:50.814 --> 00:00:53.140
that there's a disaster or an accident,

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.981
we have the data to know what was there,

00:00:55.981 --> 00:00:57.398
exactly as it is.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:02.218
We're pioneering a number of methods

00:01:02.218 --> 00:01:06.385
to return that information
into the physical world.

00:01:07.499 --> 00:01:09.259
We're doing CNC milling.

00:01:09.259 --> 00:01:10.631
We're doing 3D printing.

00:01:10.631 --> 00:01:13.548
But we're trying to go beyond that.

00:01:14.688 --> 00:01:17.389
A facsimile of the Borgherini Chapel.

00:01:17.389 --> 00:01:20.315
The facsimile of the tomb of Tutankhamen

00:01:20.315 --> 00:01:22.443
in the Valley of the Kings.

00:01:22.443 --> 00:01:27.037
An exact facsimile of
Veronese's Wedding at Cana.

00:01:27.037 --> 00:01:29.597
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:01:29.597 --> 00:01:32.347
(crowd applauds)

00:01:35.464 --> 00:01:37.735
The biggest project that's
going on at the moment

00:01:37.735 --> 00:01:41.351
is an exact facsimile
of the tomb of Seti I,

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:43.365
which will be given to the people of Egypt

00:01:43.365 --> 00:01:45.448
as soon as it's finished.

00:01:46.831 --> 00:01:50.442
200 years ago the concern
was not one of preservation.

00:01:50.442 --> 00:01:53.903
The concern was one of
Indiana Jones and discovery

00:01:53.903 --> 00:01:57.320
and excitement and cultural acquisitions.

00:01:58.772 --> 00:02:02.037
The tombs in the Valley of
the Kings lasted successfully

00:02:02.037 --> 00:02:05.599
for 3,000, three-and-
a-half thousand years.

00:02:05.599 --> 00:02:06.863
But since they've been visited,

00:02:06.863 --> 00:02:10.377
they start to decline and decay rapidly.

00:02:10.377 --> 00:02:14.209
I think the facsimile is
opening up a whole new level

00:02:14.209 --> 00:02:17.903
of possibility for display, preservation,

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:21.182
conservation, restoration, communication,

00:02:21.182 --> 00:02:25.455
dissemination of what's
important about these objects.

00:02:25.455 --> 00:02:28.725
If only we can preserve it like it is

00:02:28.725 --> 00:02:32.826
and document it and hand it
on to future generations,

00:02:32.826 --> 00:02:34.869
then there's hope.

00:02:34.869 --> 00:02:38.202
(soft orchestral music)

00:02:39.647 --> 00:02:42.564
(electronic pulse)

